-- title:
--   Slab L² norm bounded by L² norm in Iwasawa coordinates
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field. Fix $c \in [0,\infty]$ with $c \neq \infty$, together with the hypothesis that for all measurable subsets $D, D'$ of the idele group $(\mathbb{A}_F)^\times$ that are fundamental domains for the subgroup of principal ideles (the image of $F^\times$) acting on $(\mathbb{A}_F)^\times$ with respect to idelic Haar measure, and for every measurable $f : GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F) \to [0,\infty]$ invariant under left translation by the subgroup generated by the rational central and rational $\mathrm{diag}(\cdot,1)$ tori together with the full adelic unipotent subgroup, the integral of $f$, read off along chosen representatives, against the quotient measure on the corresponding orbit quotient equals $c \int_{D}\int_{D'}\int_{\mathbf{K}} f(z\,\mathrm{diag}(t,1)\,k)\,\|t\|^{-1}$, the integrations being against idelic Haar measure in $z$ and $t$ and the Haar measure of $\mathbf{K}$; here the quotient measure is the push-forward of adelic Haar measure on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ weighted by the density attached to the chosen Haar measure on the subgroup, $\mathbf{K}$ is the subgroup of elements whose finite part is integral and whose archimedean components are row isometries, and $\|\cdot\|$ is the idele norm given by the distributive Haar character. Fix further a measurable fundamental domain $D$ for the principal ideles, and a constant $V \notin \{0,\infty\}$ such that $\int_D f(\|z\|) = V\int_0^\infty f(y)\,y^{-1}$ for every measurable $f : \mathbb{R} \to [0,\infty]$; reals $0 < d_1 < d_2$; a subset $\Phi \subseteq GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$; and a homomorphism $\xi$ from the group $Z$ of the pin data $\mathtt{productionPinsOf}$ built from $\Phi$, the level-one subgroups, the local Hecke generators and the adelic box (so $Z$ is the full idele group) to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, with $\|\xi(z)\| = 1$ for all $z$. Then there exists $\kappa \neq \infty$ such that for all $\varphi, \psi : GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F) \to \mathbb{C}$ which are slab profiles for $(Z,\xi)$ — measurable, invariant under left translation by adelic upper unipotent matrices and by global points of the Borel subgroup (lower-left entry zero), transforming by $\xi$ under the central scalars in $Z$, bounded on every determinant-norm slab $\{d_1' \le \|\det g\| \le d_2'\}$ with $d_1' > 0$, and vanishing outside a band for the adelic height — the $L^2$ norm of $q \mapsto \varphi(q.\mathrm{out}) - \psi(q.\mathrm{out})$ for the quotient measure restricted to $\{q : \|\det q.\mathrm{out}\| \in [d_1,d_2]\}$ is at most $\kappa$ times the $L^2$ norm of $(t,k) \mapsto \varphi(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k) - \psi(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)$ for the product of idelic Haar measure restricted to $D$ and weighted by the density $\|t\|^{-1}$ with the Haar measure of $\mathbf{K}$.
--
--   This is the comparison of the $L^2$ norm on a determinant slab of the torus–unipotent quotient with the $L^2$ norm in Iwasawa coordinates $(t,k) \mapsto \mathrm{diag}(t,1)k$, obtained from the Iwasawa disintegration of Haar measure on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ recorded in the hypotheses on $c$ and $V$. It serves as the coordinate-comparison input to the Paley–Wiener density statement [`AutomorphicForm.exists_isSlabProfile_paleyWiener_eLpNorm_sub_restrict_rationalTorusUnipotentQuotient_lt_of_isSlabProfile`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_isSlabProfile_paleyWiener_eLpNorm_sub_restrict_rationalTorusUnipotentQuotient_lt_of_isSlabProfile).
